    "question": "When Nathan is cold, he adds an extra blanket to his bed. Each blanket warms him up by 3 degrees. One night, he was cold enough that he added half of the 14 blankets in his closet on his bed. How many degrees did the blankets warm Nathan up?",
    "gold": "21",
    "answer": "Nathan added 14 / 2 = <<14/2=7>>7 blankets to his bed.\nThe blankets warmed Nathan up 7 * 3 = <<7*3=21>>21 degrees.\n#### 21"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many degrees the blankets warmed Nathan up, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the total number of blankets Nathan added to his bed.\n2. Determine the warming effect of each blanket.\n3. Calculate the total warming effect by multiplying the number of blankets by the warming effect per blanket.\n\nFirst, we know that Nathan added half of the 14 blankets in his closet to his bed. So, we calculate:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of blankets added} = \\frac{14}{2} = 7\n\\]\n\nNext, we know that each blanket warms Nathan up by 3 degrees. Therefore, the total warming effect is:\n\\[\n\\text{Total warming effect} = 7 \\times 3 = 21\n\\]\n\nThus, the blankets warmed Nathan up by \\boxed{21} degrees.",
